  "note": "Election of the Limavady Urban Council, polled Wednesday 21 May 1952 (Belfast News-Letter, 22 May 1952, p. 5; Londonderry Sentinel, 22 May 1952, p. 3). Twelve nominations (nine official Unionists, three Independents) for nine seats (Belfast News-Letter, 8 May 1952, p. 6); eleven went to the poll. One Independent, L. E. Holmes, topped the poll and the other, H. P. M'Laughlin, was third, giving the Unionists seven seats to two. Percentage poll about 82. The two papers print Gilloway's vote as 541 (News-Letter) and 561 (Sentinel).",
  "correctionNote": "Corrected from the page images of the Belfast News-Letter, 22 May 1952, p. 5 and the Londonderry Sentinel, 22 May 1952, p. 3 (council-audit, Nov 2026): votes Walker 599 (was 699), M'Kay 588 (was 688), Moore 560 (was 660) and Kyle 525 (was 625), as both papers print and as the reported order requires (an Independent topped the poll with 619); W. Alcorn (was 'W. Bloom', an OCR misread); L. E. Holmes (was W. L.; the Sentinel prints Laurence Holmes); Kyle's initials S. N. (the News-Letter prints S. M., the Sentinel S. Nelson Kyle); Buchanan and Simpson carry the (U.) label the Sentinel prints."
